 "notes": "Libretto by Lorenzo Da Ponte (1790). Words follow the Peters engraving's spelling and punctuation: giá (as printed), finchè, quà, comediola, “vista, o si vedrà” (the o elided onto vista's last note), and Don Alfonso's “s'avanzano” (the libretto has “si avanzano”; IPA saˈvan.tsa.no). The chorus of servants and musicians (bars 23–36, “Facciam presto, o cari amici”) sings in the score and is heard with the piano, but has no role and no lines here. IPA, word meanings and translations come from the app's reviewed Così libretto drafts (L65, IPA checked against Castel), repeated where the score repeats the text; repeated fragments have short literal translations. IPA follows sung Italian conventions: stressed syllable marked, elisions (two words on one note in the score) joined with ‿, open e/o as ɛ/ɔ. Translation literal, for meaning.",
